# ── Root .npmignore — framework-footprint + secrets pack guard ──
#
# NORMALLY the package.json `files` allowlist governs the tarball and this
# file is inert for top-level selection (a root .npmignore does NOT override
# `files`; cached: learnings/stack-documentation/cli/npm-packaging.md:17).
#
# Its load-bearing role is the FALLBACK: if `files` is ever removed, npm
# consults the root .npmignore INSTEAD OF .gitignore — so a missing or
# minimal file here would ship .env / *.db / the framework footprint in
# exactly the scenario this guard exists for (S1, threat table secops.md).
# This is therefore a SUPERSET of .gitignore's sensitive entries, not a
# minimal list. Guarded by test/npmignore.test.ts.

# Secrets & credentials — never in a tarball under any configuration.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
.secret-manifest.tsv

# Local memory / SQLite stores.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Framework footprint (IP isolation — local-only, never ships).
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
framework.config.json
learnings/
stack-documentation/
PRD.json
secops.md
knowledge-map.md
LIBRARIAN.md
.librarian-fingerprint
progress.txt
.husky/
templates/
ARCHITECTURE.md
GENERICIZATION.md
docs/approved-plans/
docs/missions/
docs/case-study/
docs/SETTINGS-CHANGE-M6.md

# Dev surface — build from dist/, don't ship sources or tooling config.
# Local CLI HTML report renders (`--output html`) — dev artifacts, never shipped.
*.html
src/
test/
ci/
bin/
assets/
coverage/
.github/
.gitleaks.toml
.nvmrc
.prettierignore
.prettierrc.json
docker-compose.yml
eslint.config.mjs
tsconfig.json
tsup.config.ts
vitest.config.ts
